  "name": "Bichar gan (Bengali sung philosophical debate)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Bengali sung debate, also called pala gan, in which two singers argue opposing sides of a philosophical or religious question, such as guru and disciple, man and woman, or shariat and marifat, in alternating rounds of song before an audience, each backed by a chorus and instrumentalists. It flourishes in Manikganj, Dhaka and neighbouring districts, has a large commercial cassette and VCD output, and has been documented by the Bangla Academy. The cymbals card stands in for the small hand cymbals.",
